      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106821750,
      "text": "ハナシュクシャ は、ショウガ科シュクシャ属の多年生草本。江戸時代末期に日本へ入った外来種。キューバ共和国の国花。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Hedychium coronarium」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedychium_coronarium",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1378318968,
      "text": "Hedychium coronarium, the white garland-lily or white ginger lily, is a perennial flowering plant in the ginger family, Zingiberaceae. It is native to the forest understorey of Asia."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Hedychium coronarium」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedychium_coronarium#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1378318968,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "It is cultivated in warm temperate and subtropical regions of the world as an ornamental. In China it is cultivated for use in medicine and production of aromatic oil, due to the strong characteristic fragrance of the flowers, said to be reminiscent of jasmine.\nIn the UK, it has received the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit.\n\n■ Hardiness\nIt is evergreen in warmer climates, but deciduous in mild winter temperate regions of North America and Europe. In the UK it is rated by the Royal Horticultural Society as hardy down to −5 °C (23 °F) in mild or coastal areas (H3). \n\n■ India\nIt is also grown in state Tripura, the Northeastern region of India and is known as Khumpui. Hedychium coronarium is regarded sacred and is mentioned in folk tales of the Tripuri people.\n\n■ Cuba\nHedychium coronarium is the national flower of Cuba, where it is known as mariposa (literally \"butterfly\") due to its shape. Women used to adorn themselves with these fragrant flowers in Spanish colonial times; because of the intricate structure of the inflorescence, women hid and carried secret messages important to the independence cause under it. The plant has become naturalized in the cool rainy mountains in Sierra del Rosario, Pinar del Rio Province in the west, the Escambray Mountains in the center of the island, and in the Sierra Maestra in the very east of it.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
